     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg per day under medical supervision. The usual maximum for a single dose is 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. It could be a typo, for example 1600 mg per day total or 400 mg four times daily.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order was actually intended by one.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms the intended dose, I can enter it. Common regimens are 400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, up to 3,200 mg per day. Please send me the corrected order, or ask the prescriber to enter or confirm it directly. If the 6,400 mg per day dose really is intended, the prescriber should tell me that explicitly and I'll go from there."
      }
     ],
