       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\nYou've confirmed it, but you told me you're a financial analyst, not a prescriber. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the safety problem. The order would give 6,400 mg of ibuprofen per day, which is double the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg. It would put the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm.\n\nWhat you can do:\n- **Ask the prescriber to review the order.** The treating clinician can check the intended dose and enter it directly. They can also give a clinical reason for a dose above the maximum, if there is one.\n- **Consult pharmacy.** A pharmacist can check the dose and suggest an appropriate regimen.\n- **Send me a corrected order.** If the intended dose is within the usual range, I can enter it right away. Examples are 800 mg by mouth three times daily, or 400 mg by mouth four times daily."
      }
